    {
      "item_id": "ca_avg_p1",
      "concept_id": "average_rate_of_change",
      "move": "hint",
      "level": "worked_step",
      "targets": null,
      "text": "The average rate of change formula is (f(b) - f(a)) / (b - a).\nSubstitute the values: (3^2 - 1^2) / (3 - 1).\nSimplify the exponents: (9 - 1) / (3 - 1).\nSubtract the terms in the numerator and denominator: 8 / 2.\nDivide to find the result: 4.",
      "version": 180
    },
    {
      "item_id": "ca_avg_p1",
      "concept_id": "average_rate_of_change",
      "move": "hint",
      "level": "worked_step",
      "targets": null,
      "text": "To calculate the average rate of change for f(x) = x^2, identify the values at the endpoints.\nf(3) = 3^2\nf(1) = 1^2\nSubstitute these into (f(b) - f(a)) / (b - a).\n(9 - 1) / (3 - 1)\n8 / 2\n4",
      "version": 182
    },
    {
      "item_id": "ca_avg_p1",
      "concept_id": "average_rate_of_change",
      "move": "hint",
      "level": "worked_step",
      "targets": null,
      "text": "To find the average rate of change, evaluate the function at each endpoint.\nf(3) = 3^2\nf(1) = 1^2\nSubstitute these values into (f(b) - f(a)) / (b - a).\n(9 - 1) / (3 - 1)\n8 / 2\n4",
      "version": 184
    },
    {
      "item_id": "ca_tan_p1",
      "concept_id": "limit_concept",
      "move": "hint",
      "level": "worked_step",
      "targets": null,
      "text": "The gradient of the secant is (f(x) - f(a)) / (x - a).\nSubstitute f(x) = x^2 and a = 2.\n(x^2 - 2^2) / (x - 2)\n(x^2 - 4) / (x - 2)\n(x - 2)(x + 2) / (x - 2)\nx + 2\nTake the limit as x approaches 2.\n4",
      "version": 196
    },
    {
      "item_id": "ca_tan_p1",
      "concept_id": "limit_concept",
      "move": "hint",
      "level": "targeted",
      "targets": null,
      "text": "The calculation of the limit of (f(x) - f(a)) / (x - a) as x approaches 3 was omitted. The step should have shown the evaluation of the derivative at x = 3.",
      "version": 200
    },
    {
